# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 68-71 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 10 — CHAPTER 12, 2026-09-20; the one run): the second list (68 — headless, 12:11's words),
# the rejoicing and the Levite (69), the burnt offerings only there (70), the profane slaughter and the blood (71) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files; the
# cuts by ch12_ink.SP_; the middah where the row argues by one (checked). Chapter 11's form.
from ch12_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(68, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR BURNT OFFERINGS" (12:11) — THE INDIVIDUAL\'S AND THE COMMUNITY\'S; "YOUR SACRIFICES" — THE INDIVIDUAL\'S AND THE COMMUNITY\'S PEACE OFFERINGS. THE HEADLESS PISKA\'S FIRST ROW — its first word 12:11\'s own ({SP_(68, 1, "עולת", "יחיד", "ועולת", "צבור")} "the individual\'s and the community\'s burnt offering"): 63:6-7 said again for the second list; THE INK: 12:11\'s "your burnt offerings" plene where 12:6\'s is defective (computed) — the row\'s consonants 12:11\'s. Fresh.')
srow(68, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOUR TITHES" — R. AKIVA: TWO TITHES, OF GRAIN AND OF CATTLE (63:8 again). ({SP_(68, 2, "אחד", "מעשר", "דגן", "ואחד", "מעשר", "בהמה")} "one the tithe of grain and one the tithe of cattle"). Fresh.')
srow(68, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THE HEAVE OFFERING OF YOUR HAND" — THESE ARE THE FIRST FRUITS (63:9 again). ({SP_(68, 3, "אלו", "הבכורים")} "these are the first fruits"). Fresh.')
srow(68, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ALL THE CHOICE OF YOUR VOWS WHICH YOU VOW TO THE LORD" — TO INCLUDE VOWS AND FREEWILL OFFERINGS, THAT ONE BRING ONLY FROM THE CHOICEST. ({SP_(68, 4, "שלא", "יביא", "אלא", "מן", "המבחר")} "that he bring only from the choicest"): E1 (checked) — the second list\'s new word "choice" (12:11 the one seat — computed) made a rule of quality; Tosefta Menachot 9:2 (the English). Fresh.')
srow(68, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ONLY VOWS AND FREEWILL OFFERINGS? WHENCE TO INCLUDE FIRSTLINGS, TITHES, SIN AND GUILT OFFERINGS? "THE CHOICE OF YOUR VOWS" — "AND ALL THE CHOICE OF YOUR VOWS." ({SP_(68, 5, "מנין", "לרבות", "בכורות", "ומעשרות", "חטאות", "ואשמות")} "whence to include firstlings, tithes, sin and guilt offerings"): E1 (checked) from "all". Fresh.')
srow(68, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'RABBI: IF THEY WERE SAID ABOVE (12:6), WHY BELOW (12:11)? THE FIRST FOR SHILOH, THE SECOND FOR JERUSALEM. THE TWO LISTS AS TWO STATIONS ({SP_(68, 6, "ראשונה", "לענין", "שילה", "שניה", "לענין", "ירושלם")} "the first for Shiloh, the second for Jerusalem"): E10 (checked — the repetition read) — THE INK: the list at 12:6 and 12:11 with the items reordered and "the choice of your vows" added (computed). Fresh.')

srow(69, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL REJOICE" (12:12) — REJOICING HERE AND AT 27:7: PEACE OFFERINGS (64:2 again). The head row of piska 69 ({SP_(69, 1, "מה", "שמחה", "האמורה", "להלן", "שלמים")} "as the rejoicing said there is peace offerings"): I2 (checked). Fresh.')
srow(69, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD" — WITHIN THE PARTITION (64:1 again; the lesser holy within the wall — the English). ({SP_(69, 2, "במחיצה")} "within the partition"). Fresh.')
srow(69, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOU, YOUR SONS, YOUR DAUGHTERS, YOUR MENSERVANTS AND YOUR MAIDSERVANTS" — THE DEARER FIRST. ({SP_(69, 3, "חביב", "חביב", "קודם")} "the dearer, the dearer comes first"): the list\'s order read as rank; 74:4 says it of 12:18\'s singular list. Fresh.')
srow(69, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE LEVITE WITHIN YOUR GATES" — WHEREVER YOU FIND THIS LEVITE, GIVE HIM OF HIS PORTION; HE HAS NO PORTION — GIVE HIM THE POOR TITHE; NO POOR TITHE — GIVE HIM PEACE OFFERINGS. THE LEVITE\'S LADDER ({SP_(69, 4, "תן", "לו", "מחלקו")} "give him of his portion"; {SP_(69, 4, "תן", "לו", "מעשר", "עני")} "give him the poor tithe"): the Levite\'s three supports ranked — the first tithe (Numbers 18:21, read), the poor tithe (14:28-29, ahead), the peace offering (this chapter); THE INK: "the Levite within your gates" 12:12, 18; 14:27; 16:11 (computed). Fresh; 74:5 says it again.')

srow(70, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"TAKE HEED" (12:13) — A PROHIBITION; "LEST" — A PROHIBITION. The head row of piska 70 ({SP_(70, 1, "השמר", "בלא", "תעשה")} "take heed — a prohibition"; {SP_(70, 1, "פן", "בלא", "תעשה")} "lest — a prohibition"): the two words made a "you shall not" — the shelf\'s rule on the form (74:6-7, 81:1 again; Makkot 13b at chapter 8); THE INK: "take heed to yourself lest" three times in the chapter (computed). Fresh.')
srow(70, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"LEST YOU OFFER YOUR BURNT OFFERINGS" — YOURS, NOT THE GENTILES\' BURNT OFFERINGS: R. SHIMON; R. JUDAH: NOT THE GENTILES\' CONSECRATED OUTSIDE THE LAND. ({SP_(70, 2, "ולא", "עולות", "גוים")} "and not the burnt offerings of gentiles"): "your" a PARAMETER of the prohibition\'s subject — Mishnah Zevachim 4:5 (the English). Fresh.')
srow(70, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN EVERY PLACE THAT YOU SEE" — BUT YOU MAY OFFER IN ANY PLACE A PROPHET TELLS YOU, AS ELIJAH OFFERED ON MOUNT CARMEL. ({SP_(70, 3, "כדרך", "שהעלה", "אליהו", "בהר", "הכרמל")} "as Elijah offered on Mount Carmel"): "that you see" against the prophet\'s word — 62:1\'s procedure again; THE RUN: 1 Kings 18 the citation of the exception. Fresh.')
srow(70, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"BUT IN THE PLACE WHICH THE LORD WILL CHOOSE IN ONE OF YOUR TRIBES" (12:14) — ONE VERSE SAYS "IN ONE OF YOUR TRIBES", ANOTHER "FROM ALL YOUR TRIBES" (12:5): R. JUDAH — THE MONEY FROM ALL YOUR TRIBES, THE CHOSEN HOUSE FROM ONE TRIBE. ({SP_(70, 4, "כסף", "מכל", "שבטיכם", "בית", "הבחירה", "משבט", "אחד")} "money from all your tribes, the chosen house from one tribe"): I13 (checked) — 62:3 again; THE INK: 12:14\'s "in one of your tribes" the chapter\'s one number verse [1] (the parser). Read here first — the same words at 62:3. Fresh.')
srow(70, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"THERE YOU SHALL OFFER YOUR BURNT OFFERINGS" — ONLY BURNT OFFERINGS? THE OTHER OFFERINGS WHENCE? "AND THERE YOU SHALL DO ALL THAT I COMMAND YOU." ({SP_(70, 5, "שאר", "קרבנות", "מנין")} "the other offerings whence"): E1 (checked) from "all" — the burnt offering named, the rest included. Fresh.')
srow(70, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'STILL I MIGHT SAY: THE BURNT OFFERING IS UNDER A POSITIVE COMMAND AND A PROHIBITION, THE OTHER HOLY THINGS UNDER A POSITIVE COMMAND ALONE — "THERE YOU SHALL OFFER YOUR BURNT OFFERINGS": THE BURNT OFFERING WAS IN THE GENERAL RULE AND WENT OUT TO COMPARE TO IT — AS THE BURNT OFFERING IS UNDER BOTH, SO ALL THAT IS UNDER THE POSITIVE COMMAND IS UNDER THE PROHIBITION. ({SP_(70, 6, "עולה", "בכלל", "היתה", "ולמה", "יצאת")} "the burnt offering was in the general rule, and why did it go out"): the thing singled out to teach on the whole class — the eighth of the thirteen in form (named without a code: the row\'s "to compare to it" a hekesh); the offerings outside the place both a positive and a negative command — Zevachim 106a-107b at 10b. Fresh.')

srow(71, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONLY, WITH ALL THE DESIRE OF YOUR SOUL YOU MAY SLAUGHTER AND EAT" (12:15) — OF WHAT DOES THE VERSE SPEAK? IF OF THE FLESH OF DESIRE, IT IS SAID (12:20); IF OF EATING HOLY THINGS, IT IS SAID (12:11); IT SPEAKS ONLY OF DISQUALIFIED CONSECRATED ANIMALS THAT ARE REDEEMED. MIGHT THEY BE REDEEMED FOR A PASSING BLEMISH? "ONLY." THE VERSE ASSIGNED — the head row of piska 71 ({SP_(71, 1, "בפסולי", "המקדשים", "שיפדו")} "of disqualified consecrated animals that are redeemed"; {SP_(71, 1, "יכול", "יפדו", "על", "מום", "עובר")} "might they be redeemed for a passing blemish"): the shelf reads 12:15 not as the release from Leviticus 17 (12:20-21\'s) but as the blemished holy animal eaten as common — "only" the restriction to a permanent blemish (a PARAMETER: the blemish\'s kind); Mishnah Bekhorot 2:2 at 10b. Fresh.')
srow(71, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOU MAY SLAUGHTER AND EAT" — AND NOT SHEAR. ({SP_(71, 2, "ולא", "גזה")} "and not shearing"). Fresh.')
srow(71, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"FLESH" — AND NOT MILK. ({SP_(71, 3, "בשר", "ולא", "חלב")} "flesh and not milk"): the redeemed animal\'s wool and milk forbidden. Fresh.')
srow(71, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT THEY BE FORBIDDEN AFTER SLAUGHTER? "ACCORDING TO THE BLESSING OF THE LORD YOUR GOD WHICH HE GAVE YOU." ({SP_(71, 4, "יכול", "יהו", "אסורים", "לאחר", "זביחה")} "might they be forbidden after slaughter"). Fresh.')
srow(71, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT ANIMALS WHOSE PERMANENT BLEMISH PRECEDED THEIR CONSECRATION, REDEEMED, BE FORBIDDEN? "ONLY" (12:26 — the Hebrew\'s citation; the English reads 12:15\'s). ({SP_(71, 5, "אם", "קדם", "מום", "קבוע", "להקדשם")} "if a permanent blemish preceded their consecration"): Mishnah Bekhorot 2:2. Fresh.')
srow(71, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT THEY ARE SLAUGHTERED ONLY FOR A PERMANENT BLEMISH? A FORTIORI FROM THE FIRSTBORN — WHICH DOES NOT APPLY TO ALL OFFSPRING AND GOES OUT TO COMMON USE WITHOUT REDEMPTION, YET IS SLAUGHTERED ONLY FOR A PERMANENT BLEMISH; HOLY THINGS, WHICH APPLY TO ALL AND GO OUT ONLY BY REDEMPTION — ALL THE MORE. NO: THE FIRSTBORN\'S HOLINESS IS FROM THE WOMB AND HOLDS ON A BLEMISHED ONE. "WHICH HE GAVE YOU IN ALL YOUR GATES" — "YOUR GATES" HERE AND "YOUR GATES" AT 15:22: AS THERE ONLY FOR A PERMANENT BLEMISH, SO HERE. THE A FORTIORI REFUTED, THE ANALOGY HOLDS ({SP_(71, 6, "קל", "וחמר", "הוא")} "it is an a fortiori"; {SP_(71, 6, "שעריך", "שעריך", "לגזרה", "שוה")} "your gates, your gates — for an analogy of words"): I1 (checked) refuted, I2 (checked) on "your gates" with 15:22 (ahead — never read ahead; the firstling\'s blemish there); the row names both middot by name. Fresh; Bekhorot 15a-16a at 10b.')
srow(71, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE UNCLEAN MAY EAT" — ONLY THE UNCLEAN? THE CLEAN WHENCE? "TOGETHER THEY SHALL EAT IT" (12:22) — IT TELLS THAT BOTH EAT FROM ONE DISH. ({SP_(71, 7, "מגיד", "ששניהם", "אוכלים", "מתוך", "קערה", "אחת")} "it tells that both eat from one dish"): "the unclean and the clean" (12:15, 22; 15:22 — computed) read as one table — the common flesh needs no cleanness; 75:11 says it again. Fresh.')
srow(71, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT EVEN THE HEAVE OFFERING BE EATEN FROM ONE DISH? "TOGETHER THEY SHALL EAT IT" — THIS, NOT THE HEAVE OFFERING. ({SP_(71, 8, "ואין", "תרומה", "נאכלת", "מתוך", "קערה", "אחת")} "and the heave offering is not eaten from one dish"). Fresh.')
srow(71, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT THEY BE LIABLE FOR THE PRIESTLY GIFTS? "AS THE GAZELLE." ({SP_(71, 9, "יכול", "יהו", "חיבים", "במתנות")} "might they be liable for the gifts"): the comparison to the wild animal exempts the redeemed holy animal from the shoulder, cheeks and maw (18:3 — ahead); Chullin 10:1 at 10b. Fresh.')
srow(71, 10, 'CONTEXT', f'SHALL I EXCLUDE IT FROM THE GIFTS AND NOT FROM THE BREAST AND THIGH? "AND AS THE HART." ({SP_(71, 10, "ולא", "אוציאו", "מכלל", "חזה", "ושוק")} "and not exclude it from the class of breast and thigh"): the two animals two exclusions. Fresh.')
srow(71, 11, 'CONTEXT', f'OR AS THE GAZELLE IS WHOLLY PERMITTED (ITS FAT), SO THIS? "ONLY." ({SP_(71, 11, "יכול", "אף", "זה", "כלו", "מתר")} "might this too be wholly permitted"): the fat of the redeemed animal still forbidden — the restriction\'s third reading. Fresh.')
srow(71, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON: AS THE TORAH SET A PARTITION BETWEEN MOST HOLY AND LESSER HOLY WHEN UNBLEMISHED, DID IT SET ONE WHEN BLEMISHED? "AS THE GAZELLE AND AS THE HART" — AS THE TORAH SET NO PARTITION BETWEEN GAZELLE AND HART, SO NONE BETWEEN MOST HOLY AND LESSER HOLY WHEN BLEMISHED. ({SP_(71, 12, "כשם", "שלא", "נתנה", "תורה", "מחצה", "בין", "צבי")} "as the Torah set no partition between gazelle and hart"): the pair read as the absence of a boundary — 72:8 the counter-reading. Fresh.')
srow(71, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONLY THE BLOOD YOU SHALL NOT EAT" (12:16) — R. JUDAH: MIGHT THEY BE LIABLE FOR ITS BLOOD UNDER TWO PROHIBITIONS, LIKE THE BLOOD OF CONSECRATED ANIMALS? "ONLY THE BLOOD" — ONE PROHIBITION, NOT TWO. ({SP_(71, 13, "לאו", "אחד", "יש", "בו", "ואין", "בו", "שני", "לאוין")} "one prohibition it has, and not two"): "only" a PARAMETER of the count of prohibitions — the redeemed animal\'s blood one; Sifra Nedavah 20:7 (the English); THE INK: the plural "you (pl.) shall not eat" the one plural verb in the singular half (computed). Fresh.')
srow(71, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON THE EARTH YOU SHALL POUR IT" — NOT INTO SEAS, RIVERS OR VESSELS; "LIKE WATER" — NOT INTO WATER ITSELF; AS WATER IS PERMITTED FOR BENEFIT, SO BLOOD; AS WATER MAKES SEEDS SUSCEPTIBLE, SO BLOOD; AS WATER IS EXEMPT FROM COVERING, SO BLOOD. "LIKE WATER" READ FOUR WAYS ({SP_(71, 14, "ולא", "לתוך", "ימים", "ולא", "לתוך", "נהרות")} "and not into seas and not into rivers"; {SP_(71, 14, "מה", "מים", "מתרים", "בהניה", "אף", "דם")} "as water is permitted for benefit, so blood"): the simile made three rules — benefit, susceptibility (Mishnah Makhshirin 6:4), no covering (Mishnah Chullin 2:9 — the English); THE INK: the clause 12:16, 12:24, 15:23 (computed) — Leviticus 17:13\'s dust nowhere in it. Fresh; Chullin 83b-84a at 10b.')

assert sorted(S) == [(68, r) for r in range(1, 7)] + [(69, r) for r in range(1, 5)] + [(70, r) for r in range(1, 7)] + [(71, r) for r in range(1, 15)], sorted(S)
